# `make env` from the repo root turns this into a .env. Compose reads that .env
# from the project directory on its own, so
# nothing has to be exported in the shell or forwarded through the Makefile.
#
# .env is gitignored by bare name at any depth. This is a public repository:
# verify with `git check-ignore -v sites/repos.bythewood.me/.env`.

# There is no password here any more. Signing in happens on auth.bythewood.me,
# which pushes a code to a phone, and this site asks that one whether the cookie
# in a request is a live session. Push tokens for the git wire are unaffected:
# git cannot answer a code prompt, so those stay in this site's own database.

# Set to 0 to turn off the GitHub mirror lane. Useful for a dev run that should
# not clone 250MB before it serves a page. Anything else, including unset,
# leaves it on.
REPOS_MIRROR=
